THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
======================

No third-party source files are vendored in this repository. Every file under tavr/ and
infer.py was written for this release, so the repository carries a single license rather
than a per-directory mix. The components below are dependencies, not copies.


1. Wan2.1-T2V-14B (Alibaba Cloud / Wan team)
   Upstream: https://huggingface.co/Wan-AI/Wan2.1-T2V-14B
   License:  Apache License 2.0
   The TAVR transformer is built on the Wan2.1 architecture and its released VAE and umT5
   text encoder are loaded at inference time. Their weights are distributed separately.

2. Hugging Face Diffusers
   License:  Apache License 2.0
   Supplies the causal Wan VAE implementation that tavr/models/vae.py wraps, and the UniPC
   sampler. The pin is exact -- see requirements.txt for why.

3. Hugging Face Transformers
   License:  Apache License 2.0
   Runs the umT5 text encoder and the wav2vec 2.0 audio encoder.

4. FlashAttention 3
   Upstream: https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention
   License:  BSD 3-Clause
   The only attention backend. Built by the user; no wheel or source ships here.

5. wav2vec2-xlsr-53-espeak-cv-ft (Meta AI)
   Upstream: https://huggingface.co/facebook/wav2vec2-xlsr-53-espeak-cv-ft
   License:  Apache License 2.0
   Driving-audio features. Weights distributed separately.

6. Ultralytics YOLO
   Upstream: https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
   License:  AGPL-3.0
   Person detection during preprocessing. The package is imported at runtime and its
   yolo11x weights are loaded; neither is redistributed here. AGPL-3.0 is a copyleft
   licence whose obligations extend to software that is combined with it and conveyed or
   offered over a network. Review those terms against your own deployment, or substitute a
   detector under different terms.

7. DWPose (IDEA Research)
   Upstream: https://github.com/IDEA-Research/DWPose
   License:  Apache License 2.0
   Whole-body pose used to derive face masks. The released dw-ll_ucoco_384 ONNX weights
   are loaded at inference time and are not redistributed here.

8. ONNX Runtime
   License:  MIT
   Runs the DWPose model.


MODEL WEIGHTS
=============

The released TAVR transformer is trained on top of Wan2.1-T2V-14B (Apache License 2.0). The
weights are distributed separately; see README.md.
